  "prefLabel": "Ban 101.02 Scope",
  "priorExpiration": "1990-04-20",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ban 101.02 Scope. These rules shall apply to financial institutions that are either chartered, registered, or licensed in New Hampshire, including, without limitation:\n\n(a) Banks;\n\n(b) Trust companies;\n\n(c) Family trust companies;\n\n(d) Credit unions;\n\n(e) Small loan companies;\n\n(f) Mortgage bankers, brokers, originators, and loan servicers;\n\n(g) Motor vehicle sales finance companies;\n\n(h) Retail sellers of motor vehicles;\n\n(i) Debt adjusters;\n\n(j) Money transmitters; and\n\n(k) Other financial institutions organized and operating under the banking laws of the state of New Hampshire.\n\nSource. #1596, eff 6-30-80; ss by #2062, eff 6-25-82; ss by #2685, eff 4-20-84; EXPIRED 4-20-90\n\nNew. #6146, eff 12-22-95; ss by #10258, eff 1-24-13; ss by #14096, eff 10-3-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ban100.html"
